# The public site needs NONE of this. It builds and deploys with an empty
# environment, because no marketing page reads the session or the database.
# Everything below turns the member portal on.
#
# Copy this file to ".env" beside it and fill it in. ".env" is gitignored.
# When you add a variable here, add it to the schema in "src/env.ts" too.
#
# Production deploys require DATABASE_URL, AUTH_SECRET, and the Google OAuth
# pair — a missing one fails validation rather than shipping a broken portal.

# Postgres. buzz owns only the buzz_* tables, so this can point at an instance
# another project is already using.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:password@localhost:5432/buzz"

# Generate with: npx auth secret
AUTH_SECRET=""

# Google Cloud Console -> APIs & Services -> Credentials -> OAuth client ID,
# type "Web application". Google is the only way into the portal, local
# development included, so sign-in does nothing until these are filled in.
#
# Authorized JavaScript origins:
#   http://localhost:3000
#   https://buzzsase.vercel.app
# Authorized redirect URIs — every origin above, each with the callback suffix:
#   http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/google
#   https://buzzsase.vercel.app/api/auth/callback/google
# A missing entry is what produces "redirect_uri_mismatch".
AUTH_GOOGLE_ID=""
AUTH_GOOGLE_SECRET=""

# Who gets the officer role. Comma-separated exact addresses only. It seeds the
# role on first sign-in and promotes an existing account on its next one. It
# never demotes — removing someone here does not revoke them; edit the role
# column (or revoke their sessions) for that. Empty/unset means nobody is
# auto-promoted.
ADMIN_EMAILS=""
